cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OligoVigil, please cite the NAR Database paper (preferred) and the software archive (secondary)."
title: "OligoVigil: a curator-verified, source-anchored database of safety and off-target evidence for therapeutic oligonucleotides"
type: software
abstract: >-
  OligoVigil is a no-login web portal and database of curator-verified
  preclinical safety and off-target evidence for therapeutic
  oligonucleotides (ASO, siRNA, PMO, LNA, aptamer, GalNAc-siRNA). The v1
  release contains 737 human-adjudicated records (626 toxicity + 111
  off-target) from 660 primary sources, each anchored to an exact
  in-source location and graded A/B/C, plus a leakage-aware 344-record
  evaluation benchmark with deterministic prior baselines. Following the
  v6 within-team collaborator round (2026-06-07), placeholder benchmark
  contamination was reduced from 31.1% to 4.1% and new chemistry and
  delivery dimensions were added. A second-round toxicity expansion
  (EXPAND-2; +32 records) and a mixed-sample inter-rater study with an
  independent second curator (KAPPA-2) followed: Cohen kappa_binary =
  0.42 under the drop-abstain convention and 0.34 under a
  safety-conservative collapse-abstain convention.
  The candidate-to-release firewall (no machine output is presented as
  human curation) and the full curation audit trail are exposed as bulk
  downloads and via a documented REST API with OpenAPI / MCP / Bioschemas
  JSON-LD / W3C PROV interfaces.
